From e5a87c7c85900c64aa628057ccccc1756047a888 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adrien Delmas <adrien@adriendelmas.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 19:19:14 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 177/181] hydra: cycles:denoise_aovs, OIDN on the render vars
 listed

As the AOVs list of Karma's denoiser: the render vars named in
cycles:denoise_aovs (spaces or commas; Cycles Render Settings LOP, AOVs
tab, Denoise AOVs) are denoised by OIDN on the CPU when the render ends,
guided by albedo and normal passes the delegate adds under names it can
read. The beauty and the reads of it stay with Cycles' own denoiser when
it is on. Cycles sends one more progressive update after the final
write; it now leaves a denoised AOV alone. Measured against 2048 spp,
64 spp: a light group lit by bounces 0.00736 -> 0.00206 RMSE; one made
of fine direct splat emission 0.00347 -> 0.00442 (OIDN takes the detail
for noise), so the list is the user's choice per pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
